      "output": "## The animation: what was read\n\nAll six files were read, checked and handed on unchanged; every publish receipt gave the same SHA-256 as the one computed from the input.\n\n**Checks that ran**\n- `read_sources.py` did all of step 1 in one script. Its first run stopped because I had not expected the acts' beat keys to be named `from` / `to`; the second run finished.\n- The archive unpacked with `tarfile`: 11 files (`timeline.json`, `film.py`, `anim/events.json`, `anim/common.py` and the seven act scripts).\n- Each copy at the top of the workspace was hashed again before publishing: 6 of 6 equal to the input.\n\n### Timeline (`timeline.json`)\n- 25 frames a second, 660 frames, 26.4 s (the file's `seconds`, and 660 / 25).\n- 140.0 beats a minute, first hit at 0.449 s; one beat is 0.4286 s, 10.71 frames.\n- Beat 0 falls on frame 11; the file says frames 0-11 before it are black with a glint.\n\n### Acts\nframe = round((first_hit + beat × 60 / bpm) × fps)\n\n| Act | Beats | Frames | Seconds | Script lines |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| open | 0-8 | 11-97 | 0.449-3.878 | 194 (`anim/open.py`) |\n| hero | 8-16 | 97-183 | 3.878-7.306 | 55 (`anim/hero.py`) |\n| exploded | 16-24 | 183-268 | 7.306-10.735 | 210 (`anim/exploded.py`) |\n| inside | 24-34 | 268-376 | 10.735-15.020 | 301 (`anim/inside.py`) |\n| break | 34-40 | 376-440 | 15.020-17.592 | 123 (`anim/break.py`) |\n| second | 40-52 | 440-568 | 17.592-22.735 | 297 (`anim/second.py`) |\n| lockup | 52-60.55 | 568-660 | 22.735-26.399 | 125 (`anim/lockup.py`) |\n\n- The lockup's last beat gives frame 660, which is the frame count, so it is the end bound; the last frame drawn is 659.\n- Not acts, but in the archive: `anim/common.py` 174 lines, `film.py` 394 lines.\n\n### Events (`anim/events.json`)\n- 60 events, and the file gives kinds: whoosh 18, tick 15, whirr 10, impact 8, seat 6, windup 2, glitch 1.\n- By act: exploded 16, second 14, inside 11, break 7, open 7, hero 3, lockup 2.\n\n### Sheet 03, as viewed (one view, picture returned)\n- A 4 × 4 grid of frames of the exploded view: the joint pulled apart along its axis on black, numbered leader tags (STATOR 24-SLOT, ROTOR 28-POLE, HOLLOW SHAFT, 24 PINS, CYCLOID DISC A/B and others) and a large PART GROUPS counter rising 02, 05, 08, 12, 14, 15.\n- The last row is a motion-blurred whip of the camera, then three frames of a bright ring around a dark bore with a crosshair.\n\n### What the motion language allows\n- Five curves (enter, move, exit, emphasis for one hero moment at a time, linear only for what never starts or stops), four durations (0.08 / 0.2 / 0.44 / 0.88 s), three springs (seat, glide, land) and cascades a quarter of a beat apart. The motor and the camera always move; words, the landed wordmark and the horizon hold still.\n- Transitions go only through the mechanism, with three exceptions used once each: the glitch cut on beat 37, the one-frame change of ground on beat 50, and the drawn closing on beat 52. At most 3 full-frame flashes a second, and frame 0 is a finished picture.\n\n### Not in the files\n- `motion-tokens.json`, which the motion language says sits beside it, is not among the attached files or in the archive.\n- The film's frames themselves are present only as the four sheets (01, 03, 05, 07); only sheet 03 was looked at.\n\n### Files handed on\n\n| Name | Bytes | SHA-256 (first 12) | Same bytes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| onda-k2-film-sheet-01.jpg | 146319 | `47afaf48dc48` | same bytes: yes |\n| onda-k2-film-sheet-03.jpg | 348021 | `0d065853d84c` | same bytes: yes |\n| onda-k2-film-sheet-05.jpg | 401512 | `16b0558e5ac4` | same bytes: yes |\n| onda-k2-film-sheet-07.jpg | 285370 | `c1b1ddad5bb5` | same bytes: yes |\n| onda-k2-motion-language.md | 5583 | `af0243079cb3` | same bytes: yes |\n| onda-k2-motion-src.tar.gz | 41021 | `ec6361c0fc88` | same bytes: yes |",
