      "outputType": "markdown",
      "output": "## The 2D layer: what was read\n\nAll four files were handed on unchanged, and each publish receipt's SHA-256 equals the one computed from the input. One script (`read_layer.py`) hashed the inputs, unpacked the archive with `tarfile` (10 members, 10 files) and read `comp/SHOTS.md`, the JavaScript lengths and `compose.py`. It was run several times with different views to keep each print under 60 lines.\n\n### Shots the layer draws (from `comp/SHOTS.md`, 124 lines, 7 acts)\n\nThe file states every moment as a beat. The frame numbers are what those beats come to \"today\" (beat 0 is frame 11, and the film is 660 frames).\n\n| # | Act | Beats | Frames | What the layer draws |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | open (black) | 0-8 | 0-96 | ONDA huge for two frames on the first hit. Three tags, one per shot: 24 PINS, CYCLOID DISC A, HOLLOW SHAFT. A crosshair rides each tagged part. |\n| 2 | hero (black) | 8-16 | 97-182 | K2 in vermilion italic for two frames. CYCLOIDAL JOINT wipes open from the left. The claim REDUCTION 23:1 rises on a graphite veil. |\n| 3 | exploded (black) | 16-24 | 183-267 | 15 numbered tags, one per part group, come out in a cascade with 36 px labels in two waves. A counter steps 01 to 15, then holds as 15 PART GROUPS. A calliper closes on the stator, the rotor and the shaft, with a crosshair on its sliding jaw. Everything has drawn back by beat 23.6. |\n| 4 | inside (black) | 24-34 | 268-375 | 20 mm for two frames. Dive rings and a crosshair down the bore. The claim 24 PINS / 23 LOBES. A drawing of the cycloid stage that wobbles with the rendered motor's angle. Tags ROTOR 28-POLE, STATOR 24-SLOT and ENCODER 19-BIT, the last with 19 cells counting in binary. Two-frame accents 24-SLOT, 28-POLE, 19-BIT. No tag in the pin shot. |\n| 5 | break (black, joint dimmed) | 34-40 | 376-439 | A veil dims the joint (0.5, then 0.66). The picture tears into slanted bands and lattice blocks. One burst of column noise and one vertical roll. The word PEAK cut in 11 bands. Readout windows pile up in four piles. The figure 162 N·m with PEAK on a vermilion plate. The kick on the cut at beat 37. No full-frame flash. |\n| 6 | second | 40-52 | 440-567 | K2 for two frames. The calliper hugs all the parts, with the readout 15/15. 15 PART GROUPS holds. A 23:1 outline accent. The claim LOST MOTION 0.00 arcmin. K2 tags on the elbow and the shoulder. The field is vermilion, then bone on beat 50. QUIET (thin italic) and FORCE. (fat roman) are printed on the field, knocked out to outlines where the joint covers them. The joint's contact shadow and off-register shadow. The protractor is listed but \"not drawn today\". |\n| 7 | lockup (black) | 52-60.55 | 568-659 | The bone field closes into the top rail. Two hairline rails at y 120 and y 876. A line of six number cells: 24 / 23, 23:1, 162 N·m, 0.00 arcmin, 19-BIT, 15. The ONDA wordmark drops and lands on beat 56. K2 and the tagline QUIET FORCE. wipe open after it. No type stands in the joint's place. |\n\n### The layer's files (lengths in lines)\n\n| File | Lines | Bytes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `comp/shots.js` | 789 | 47,082 |\n| `comp/tags.js` | 394 | 18,185 |\n| `comp/plates.js` | 277 | 13,749 |\n| `comp/backdrops.js` | 251 | 11,421 |\n| `comp/type.js` | 178 | 9,547 |\n| `comp/main.js` | 70 | 2,859 |\n| `comp/accents.js` | 43 | 2,592 |\n| **JavaScript total (7 files)** | **2,002** | |\n| `comp/index.html` (one canvas `#film`, loads `./main.js` as a module) | 16 | 380 |\n| `comp/SHOTS.md` | 124 | 16,823 |\n| `compose.py` | 54 | 3,310 |\n\n### How the layer is put over the frames (`compose.py`)\n\nIn a line: `compose.py` serves the case folder on 127.0.0.1, where the page finds the rendered 3D plates (`frames/3d/f%06d.png`) and `frames/anchors.json` and \"draws over and behind them\".\n\n- **Capture:** `tools/capture.mjs` captures the page frame by frame into `out/comp-<tag>/`.\n- **Encode:** ffmpeg encodes `out/onda-k2-<tag>.mp4` as H.264, BT.709 tagged, with `out/sound/mix.wav` (AAC) cut to the same range.\n- **Defaults named in its usage line:** `--size 1920x1080`, `--crf 14`.\n\nThis comes from the file's own description and its server, capture and ffmpeg lines.\n\n### What is not in the files, or was not read\n\n- **Named but not in the archive:** `tools/capture.mjs`, `tools/timing.mjs`, `tools/flashes.py`, `tools/gpu_queue.py`, `../timeline.json`, `MOTION.md`, `DECISIONS-2d.md`, the 3D plates and `frames/anchors.json`.\n- **Not read:** the bodies of the JavaScript files; only their lengths were measured. How the page blends a plate inside the canvas is therefore not stated here.\n- **Not run:** the page itself, which needs the plates.\n- **Not looked at:** the exploded and lockup style frames; they were only hashed and copied.\n\n### Look: `onda-k2-layer-poster.jpg` (viewed once; the picture was returned, 1920x1080)\n\nA grained vermilion field carries QUIET in thin bone italic above FORCE. in fat black roman, both print-worn, with a small header ONDA K2 / CYCLOIDAL JOINT and corner marks.\nThe joint (vermilion flange, bolted silver face, black finned body with an ice-blue ring) stands in front at the right with a shadow, and the letters it covers (the T, and R, C, E) show through it as bone outlines.\n\n### Files handed on\n\n| Name | Bytes | SHA-256 (first 12) | Receipt |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `onda-k2-layer-exploded.jpg` | 266,476 | `9afcc9cb6c4a` | same bytes: yes |\n| `onda-k2-layer-lockup.jpg` | 250,572 | `7209ac7a79e8` | same bytes: yes |\n| `onda-k2-layer-poster.jpg` | 573,784 | `96b67ee80962` | same bytes: yes |\n| `onda-k2-layer-src.tar.gz` | 42,365 | `324430064485` | same bytes: yes |\n\nEach was published once; no file needed a second copy or publish.",
