      "outputType": "markdown",
      "output": "## The sound of ONDA K2: what was read and handed on\n\nAll four files were read, measured and handed on unchanged; every publish receipt's SHA-256 equals the one computed from the input. Nothing was decoded or listened to, so nothing here says how the files sound.\n\n### Cues (`out/sound/cues.json`)\n\n- **263 cues in all**, in **26 kinds** (the counts sum to 263):\n\n| kind | n | kind | n | kind | n | kind | n |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| pulse | 52 | window | 14 | flash | 6 | stutter | 2 |\n| count | 32 | glint | 13 | calliper | 4 | whip | 2 |\n| tag | 31 | fly | 11 | word | 3 | windup | 2 |\n| whoosh | 21 | impact | 9 | drop | 2 | glitch | 1 |\n| roll | 20 | seat | 9 | servo | 2 | motor | 1 |\n| tick | 15 | slice | 7 | | | riser | 1 |\n| | | | | | | spike | 1 |\n| | | | | | | tapestop | 1 |\n| | | | | | | tone | 1 |\n\n- **By layer:** 2d 103, 3d 71, sound 56, decor 33.\n- **By `src`:** guess 192, events 71.\n- **By act:** open 25, hero 15, exploded 71, inside 49, break 37, second 38, lockup 28.\n- **Also in the file:** `bpm` 140.0, `first_hit` 0.449, and a separate list of 765 events. Cue beats run from -1.048 to 60.\n\n### Voices and cue kinds by name (names only)\n\n- **`synth.py`, 16 voices:** seat, tick, whoosh, blip, glint, motor, room_tone, crush, stutter, tapestop, growl, pulse, flash, riser, subdrop, impact. These are exactly the 16 values of the cues' `fx` field, and each is a function defined in `synth.py`.\n- **`synth.py`, other functions:** the remaining 20 top-level functions (filters, envelopes, panning, reverb and the like, such as `bp`, `lp`, `hp`, `decay`, `reverb`) are called by other `synth.py` functions. I take them as helpers by that fact, not by reading their bodies.\n- **`cues.py`, 28 cue makers** (functions named `_<kind>`; that they are the makers is my reading of the naming): calliper, count, drop, flash, fly, glint, glitch, hit, impact, motor, pulse, riser, roll, seat, select, servo, slice, spike, stutter, tag, tapestop, tick, tone, whip, whoosh, window, windup, word.\n- **Against the cue list:** all 26 kinds in `cues.json` have a maker of that name. Two makers, `hit` and `select`, have no cue of that kind in `cues.json`.\n- **Rest of the archive:** it holds 9 files. Besides the three above: `audition.py`, `levels.py`, `mix.py`, `musickey.py`, `picture.py`, `test_events.py`. These were listed only; I did not read them for content and did not run them.\n\n### The MP3s against the film's 26.4 s\n\nMPEG frames were counted in Python from each frame header; no bytes were left unparsed.\n\n| file | audio frames | seconds (frames x 1152 / 48000) | after the trim its header declares | bit rate | against 26.4 s |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| onda-k2-mix.mp3 | 1101 | 26.424 | 26.400 | 192 kbit/s, constant | +0.024 s raw, 0.000 s trimmed |\n| onda-k2-music.mp3 | 1101 | 26.424 | 26.400 | 192 kbit/s, constant | +0.024 s raw, 0.000 s trimmed |\n| onda-k2-sfx.mp3 | 1101 | 26.424 | 26.400 | 192 kbit/s, constant | +0.024 s raw, 0.000 s trimmed |\n\n- **Format:** each is MPEG-1 Layer 3, 48,000 Hz, 2 channels, with a 44-byte ID3v2 tag and one extra `Info` header frame (1102 frames in the file).\n- **The 0.024 s:** the `Info` frame declares an encoder delay of 576 samples and padding of 576 samples. A player that honours it plays 1,267,200 samples, which is 26.400 s; one that does not plays 26.424 s.\n- **Same size, different files:** the three MP3s are the same byte size because they share length and constant bit rate. Their SHA-256 values differ.\n\n### Not in the files, or not checked\n\n- **Mix against stems:** not checked. That would need decoding, and there is no decoder here.\n- **Levels, loudness, peaks, sync to picture:** not measured.\n- **Where the music comes from:** I did not establish whether or where the archive synthesizes the music stem. I took only names from `cues.py` and `synth.py`, as asked.\n\n### Files handed on\n\n| name | bytes | SHA-256 (first 12) | same bytes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| onda-k2-mix.mp3 | 634,796 | `9b6f6a54172e` | same bytes: yes |\n| onda-k2-music.mp3 | 634,796 | `557f039e528c` | same bytes: yes |\n| onda-k2-sfx.mp3 | 634,796 | `4233604c9c34` | same bytes: yes |\n| onda-k2-sound-src.tar.gz | 54,535 | `80be1c16877e` | same bytes: yes |\n\n### Checks that ran\n\n- **`read_sound.py`:** one script that unpacked the archive with `tarfile`, counted the cues, took the names by `ast`, counted the MPEG frames and computed the four SHA-256 values. Its first run stopped on a `tarfile` argument this Python lacks; after the fix it ran clean.\n- **Copies:** `cmp` found each copy identical to its input.\n- **Publishes:** four, each receipt's full SHA-256 equal to the computed one on the first try. No file was republished.",
